    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>As a leprous, devout street child in Damascus, Ibn Ja'far was bestowed the legendary golden coin of the Prophet on Salah al-Din's deathbed in 1193, ahead of the sultan's own family &mdash; a sign the Hajj took as a divine mandate to Embrace him rather than the dying sultan himself. Upon his Embrace his skin took on a permanent sooty-gold luster, and he was sent to found a new khitta of the Hajj in Cairo, the city of Salah al-Din's greatest triumph. For centuries he served as the very model of the Ashirra's religious authority &mdash; beneficent, capable, admired.</p><p>In recent decades Ibn Ja'far has lost his golden coin, and with it, he fears, his faith and his purpose. He confides this crisis only in his childe Shahid, and his once-fiery sermons have grown hollow. He remains councilor of Cairo and the acknowledged leader of both the Hajj and the wider Ashirra sect (which numbers 80-100 vampires in the city), but his spiritual paralysis leaves the sect's considerable influence effectively rudderless at a dangerous moment.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Portray Ibn Ja'far as a Messianic figure hollowed out by doubt &mdash; still commanding, still deeply learned in Islamic theology, but privately consumed by the fear that his existence and his faith were always inseparable from a relic he has now lost.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Ja'far al-Medinat. Childe: Shahid, Keeper of the Word (his closest confidant). Rival: Shagaret al-Durr, the Tree of Pearls, who leads the non-Muslim @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.UhaIbwzsC1O2x9vr]{Nosferatu} cult the Alnilam within Cairo's @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.UhaIbwzsC1O2x9vr]{Nosferatu} and secretly schemes against the prince. Note: this book's original stat block substitutes Dur-An-Ki (Mesopotamian Blood Magic, detailed in Blood Sacrifice) for standard Thaumaturgy at the Storyteller's discretion; treat this as Thaumaturgy (Path of Blood 5, Path of Spirit Manipulation 2) if using this book alone. True Faith: formerly 5, currently 0.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
